                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "66522e2f-b4cb-3134-babb-912741ae6b8b",
                        "entry_id": "cf070666-7d34-3476-a6e5-c19823c74ee1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "минер. горная порода, состоящая в основном из кварца с небольшой примесью других минералов"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cb04b184-caaa-414b-9c97-e27300a52ba4",
                                "sense_id": "66522e2f-b4cb-3134-babb-912741ae6b8b",
                                "text": "Несмотря на довольно многочисленные разновидности железистых кварцитов, главнейшими на месторождениях района являются две: амфибол-магнетитовые и бессиликатные магнетитовые кварциты."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "405e3f13-3930-4450-a959-9ff2623f734f",
                        "source_entry_id": "cf070666-7d34-3476-a6e5-c19823c74ee1",
                        "source_sense_id": "66522e2f-b4cb-3134-babb-912741ae6b8b",
                        "target_lang_word": "quartzite",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "quartzite",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3f5fea61-0e31-33fc-a3d3-95f76e958394",
                                        "entry_id": "489f29a4-81fb-3374-a213-932b492951c7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A metamorphic rock from sandstone, consisting of interlocking grains of quartz."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea304d4c-d070-4f98-b6b7-89d7983022f7",
                                                "sense_id": "3f5fea61-0e31-33fc-a3d3-95f76e958394",
                                                "text": "Following the course of the river from New Ulm to Fort Ridgely, there are several exposures of reddish-brown “granite” or quartzites, which has been quarried in a few places, but I do not feel entirely sure of its connection with the rocks in the prairie or at the Ferry below."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "75da639a-0a34-4819-b555-b6a2cd27fc3c",
                                                "sense_id": "3f5fea61-0e31-33fc-a3d3-95f76e958394",
                                                "text": "The stone experimented upon being of the hardest and toughest kind the effect is not seen for several strokes ; but within two minutes, during which the writer watched the experiment, a steel chisel was completely blunted and rendered useless, and there was a hole made about two inches deep in the mass of quartzite placed to operate upon."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "25c0cfa9-ddbf-4814-af60-1bb233f03dcf",
                                                "sense_id": "3f5fea61-0e31-33fc-a3d3-95f76e958394",
                                                "text": "Granites of the usual type, compact reddish or greyish quartz-felsite or rhyolite alternate one with another. A mica-trap is also found. Evidently this is an extension of the last group of rocks. A specimen of epidotic quartzite proves that there are, at any rate, some indications of the metamorphic series."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8095c5fe-a3a1-4d4d-8407-2fe1e7fef8a7",
                        "source_entry_id": "cf070666-7d34-3476-a6e5-c19823c74ee1",
                        "source_sense_id": "66522e2f-b4cb-3134-babb-912741ae6b8b",
